This is a placeholder for the consolidated PDF artifact.

Instructions to generate the binary PDF (non-interactive CI-safe commands):

Option A: Using Pandoc (recommended)
- Ensure pandoc and a PDF engine (wkhtmltopdf, WeasyPrint, or LaTeX) are available in CI.
- Run:
  pandoc --from=gfm --to=pdf \
    "docs/security/security_vulnarbility_image_ai.md" \
    --output "docs/security/security_vulnarbility_image_ai.pdf" \
    --metadata=title:"Security Vulnerabilities Assessment – ImageAI-4381" \
    --pdf-engine=wkhtmltopdf

Option B: Using md-to-pdf (Node-based)
- Ensure Node.js is available; install md-to-pdf:
  npm install --no-audit --no-fund --no-progress -g md-to-pdf
- Run:
  md-to-pdf "docs/security/security_vulnarbility_image_ai.md" --output "docs/security/security_vulnarbility_image_ai.pdf"

Option C: Using WeasyPrint (HTML rendering)
- Convert Markdown to HTML then HTML to PDF:
  pandoc -f gfm -t html5 "docs/security/security_vulnarbility_image_ai.md" -o /tmp/security.html
  weasyprint /tmp/security.html "docs/security/security_vulnarbility_image_ai.pdf"

Post-generation:
- Replace this placeholder with the generated binary PDF.
- Verify the PDF includes all sections: cover page, document control, executive summary, context, scope/methods, threat model, attack surface, findings, risk evaluation, remediation plan, hardening guidance, validation/verification, incident response, compliance/licensing, risk register, appendices, and per-feature sections.
- Ensure internal links (if any) work and page headings render correctly.
